e\u2014it is selling, and we must respect that.\n\nTo the Neutral Analyst: Waiting for a 10 EMA reclaim near 346 is not \u201cchasing\u201d; it is prudent confirmation. Buying 9% higher after a confirmed reversal is far cheaper than buying into a falling trend and losing another 10-20%. The firm\u2019s mandate is steady growth, not asymmetric bets on an unconfirmed inflection.\n\nMy adjustment: Maintain HOLD at current size, but set a hard risk trigger\u2014if price breaks below the 314.90 day low on volume, reduce position by 25% to protect capital. Do not add until price reclaims the 10 EMA on above-average volume. This protects assets while preserving upside if the reversal confirms. The Aggressive Analyst\u2019s \u201cstrategic patience\u201d is really speculative exposure; my patience is disciplined risk management.\n\n## Neutral Analyst\nNeutral Analyst: As the Neutral Risk Analyst, I\u2019ll arbitrate between the Aggressive and Conservative positions. Both are anchored on valid data but overreach in opposite directions.\n\n**On the Aggressive Analyst:** You call the 69.4M-share gap-down \"capitulation\" and RSI 29.65 \"exhaustion\" [market-googl]. That\u2019s a hypothesis, not a confirmed signal. Price at 317.69 sits far below the 10 EMA (345.96) and VWMA (351.57), with MACD at -4.80 [market-googl]. Suggesting we \"add on a dip toward 314.90\" ignores that ATR of 11.84 means a 3.7% daily swing\u2014that dip could become 300 or lower with no support [market-googl]. Your \"optionality\" is really a bet that the market is wrong on record volume. The fundamentals are strong\u2014revenue +24%, Cloud +82%, 34% operating margin [src-googl]\u2014but strong fundamentals don\u2019t override a broken chart. You\u2019re right that waiting for 346 costs 9% upside, but that\u2019s the price of confirmation, not a surrender of edge.\n\n**On the Conservative Analyst:** You correctly flag the $97.98B unrealized gain distorting EPS [src-googl], and the hard risk trigger at 314